","Hemoglobin E disorders are a group of inherited disorders characterized by a mutation in the β-globin gene, which leads to the production of an abnormal hemoglobin variant called hemoglobin E. These disorders are associated with varying clinical presentations, from mild to severe, depending on the inheritance pattern. The interaction with β-thalassemia is critical in determining the severity of the condition.  

