","The inhibition of signal-induced transcription by wortmannicin, Ly294002, and BX795 indicates that the signaling pathway involves the activation of phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase (PI3K) and the subsequent activation of Akt (also known as protein kinase 1), which phosphorylates and activates downstream transcription factors. Thus, the two enzymes implicated are:  
