- The middle layer (fibrotendinous layer) is the main part of the tendon, with tightly packed collagen fibers.  
- The inner layer (endotendon) is smooth and vascular.  

**Function of Tendons:**  
Tendons allow muscles to move bones by providing a strong, flexible connection between the two. When a muscle contracts, it pulls on the tendon, which in turn moves the bone.  

