In summary, neurodegenerative diseases can affect the transmission of signals between neurons in the brain through various mechanisms, including disruption of neurotransmitter systems, damage to synapses, accumulation of toxic proteins, damage to myelin, and loss of neurons. These changes can lead to a decline in cognitive and motor function, as well as other neurological symptoms.",fluency,"# Task Description
