   2 CH3COOH (l) + 3 O2 (g) → 2 CO2 (g) + 2 H2O (l)  
   
   The balanced equation for the combustion of ethanol is:  
   C2H5OH (l) + 1.5 O2 (g) → CH3CO(OH) (l) + 2 H2O (l)  
   
