For H\(_2\)SO\(_4\), the normality is twice the molarity, since it is a dibasic acid (2 H\(_2\)O groups per molecule).
Thus, \( \text{N} = 2 \times \text{M} \).

First, we calculate the molarity of the 2.00 N H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) solution:
\[
