   \]
   \[
   \text{Mass of NaCl} = 5 \text{ g} \times 0.85 = 4.25 \text{ g}
   \]

2. **Interpretation of the question:**
   The question asks how much NaCl can be ""obtained"" from the sample. Since the sample is 85% NaCl, the amount of NaCl obtained is the same as the mass of NaCl in the sample.

3. **Conclusion:**
   The amount of NaCl that can be obtained from the 5 g of sea salt is \(\boxed{4.25 \text{ g}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

