   \[
   Zn(s) + Cu^{2+}(aq) \rightarrow Zn^{2+}(aq) + Cu(s)
   \]
   Two electrons are transferred in the oxidation of \( Zn \) to \( Zn^{2+} \) and two electrons are accepted in the reduction of \( Cu^{2+} \) to \( Cu \).
   Thus, \( n = 2 \).

3. **Calculate the Gibbs free energy change (\( \Delta G \))**:
   Substitute the values into the formula:
   \[
   \Delta G = -n F \Delta E = -2 \times 96,410 \, \text{C/mol} \times 1.10 \, \text{V} = -212,822 \, \text{J/mol}
   \]
   Convert to kJ/mol:
