- The system reliability function is the product of the individual component reliability functions:  
\[ R_S(t) = R_1(t) \times R_2(t) \times R_3(t) \times R_4(t) \times R_5(t) = \prod_{i=1}^5 R_i(t) \]  
This means the system is only as reliable as the least reliable component.  

**b) Parallel Structure**  
In a parallel system, the system is operational if any component is operational. The system fails only if all components fail.  
