\]
\[
55 = 90 - \text{Number with }G \text{ and } P
\]
\[
\text{Number with }G \text{ and } P = 90 - 55 = 35
\]
Thus, the number of houses with both a two-car garage and an in-the-ground swimming pool is 35.

Alternatively, we can use the principle of complementary counting.
The number of houses with either a two-car garage or an in-the-ground swimming pool is the total number of houses minus the number of houses with neither, which is $90 - 35 = 55$.
