The initial kinetic energy is \( K_i = \frac{1}{2}mv^i^2 \), and the final kinetic energy is \( K_f = \frac{1}{2}mv^f^2 \).
Substituting \( v_f = \frac{1}{3} v_i \), we get
\[ K_F = \frac{1}{2}m(\frac{1}{3} v_i)^2 = \frac{1}{2}m\left(\frac{1}{9} v_i^2\right) = \frac{1}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}mv_i^2\right) = \frac{1}{9} K_i \]
The fraction of kinetic energy lost is
\[ \frac{K_i - K_F}{K_i} = 1 - \frac{K_F}{K_i} = 1 - \frac{1}{9} = \frac{8}{9} \]

