   \[
   \frac{A_v'}{A_v} = \frac{1}{2^{6}} = \frac{1}{64}
   \]
   Thus, the new open-loop gain is:
   \[
   A_v' = \frac{A_v}{64} = \frac{100}{64} = 1.58 \, \text{V/V}
   \]

3. **Calculate the new closed-loop gain \( A_{vf}' \)**:
   Using the same feedback factor \( m_v = 0.1 \), the new closed-loop gain is:
   \[
   A_{vf}' = \frac{A_v'}{1 - m_v} = \frac{1.58}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{1.58}{0.9} \approx 1.69 \, \text{V/V}
   \]

4. **Calculate the percentage change in the closed-loop gain**:
   \[
   \Delta A_{vf} = \left( \frac{A_{vf}' - A_{vf^{(0)}}{ A_{vf}^{(0)}} \right) \times 100\% = \left( \frac{1.69 - 109.09}{109.09} \right) \times 100\%
