1. **Given Data:**  
   - Mass \( m = 1.2 \, \text{kg} \).  
   - Density \( \rho = 7150 \, \text{kg/m}^3 \).  
   - Surface area \( A = 0.075 \, \text{m}^2 \).  
   - Thermal conductivity \( k = 95 \, \text{W/mK} \).  
   - Specific heat \( c = 385 \, \, \text{J/kg K} \).  
   - Initial temperature \( T_0 = 345 \, \text{°C} = 372 \, \text{K} \).  
   - Ambient temperature \( T_{\infty} = 20 \, \text{C} = 293 \, \text{K}).  
   - Convective heat transfer coefficient \( h = 56.8 \, \text{W/m}^2 \text{K} \).  

2. **Calculations:**  
   - **Volume \( V \):**  
     \[
     V = \frac{m}{\rho} = \frac{1.2 \, \text{kg}}{7150 \, \text{kg/m}^3} = 0.00166 \, \text{m}^3
     \]  
